/TU (Part 9\056 General Eligibility and Inadmissibility Grounds\056 Criminal Acts and Violations\056 For Item Numbers 22\056 \055 41\056\054 you must answer \042Yes\042 to any question that applies to you\054 even if your records were sealed or otherwise cleared\054 or even if anyone\054 including a judge\054 law enforcement officer\054 or attorney\054 told you that you no longer have a record\056 You must also answer \042Yes\042 to the following questions whether the action or offense occurred here in the United States or anywhere else in the world\056  If you answer \042Yes\042 to Item Numbers 22\056 \055 41\056\054 use the space provided in Part 14\056 Additional Information to provide an explanation for each offense\054 if applicable\054 that includes a description of the criminal offense\073 where the criminal offense occurred\073 when the criminal offense occurred\073 whether you were arrested\054 cited\054 charged\054 or detained for the criminal offense you committed\073 and the outcome or disposition of that criminal offense \050for example\054 convicted\054 placement in a diversion program\054 no charges filed\054 charges dismissed\054 jail\054 prison\054 detention\054 probation\054 or community service\051\056 Your explanation must include the duration of any sentence to confinement \050even if suspended\051\056 22\056 Have you EVER been arrested\054 cited\054 charged\054 or permitted to participate in a diversion program \050including pre\055trial diversion\054 deferred prosecution\054 deferred adjudication\054 or any withheld adjudication\051\054 or detained for any reason by any law enforcement official in any country including but not limited to any U\056S\056 immigration official or any official of the U\056S\056 armed forces or U\056S\056 Coast Guard or by a similar official of a country other than the United States\077 Select Yes\056 )
/Type /Annot
